<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93993" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῐγύνης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spear</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.152
			</span></i>; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίγῡνος</span></b> ,
				ὁ, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.99
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.176
			</span></i> codd. (<i><span class="en">
				Maced.
			</span></i>); <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίγῡνον</span></b> , τό, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1457b6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.578
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); and in <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				556
			</span></i>, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίγυμνον</span></b>  (in dat.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῳ</span>).—Cyprian acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> cc., Scythian acc. to Sch.Par.<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.320
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				111
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιγύͅνης</span> among the Ligyes near
			Marseilles was used for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάπηλος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σιγύνναι, οἱ</span>, a people on the Middle Danube, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> l.c.; in <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.320
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σίγυννοι</span>; in <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				11.11.8
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σίγιννοι</span>. [In <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span>; freq. written
			with double <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
				σιγύννης</span>, etc.]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
